.TH PHASORSTD_ARRAY 3 "July 2026" "Phasor 4.0.0" "Phasor Standard Library 4.0.0"
.SH NAME
phasorstd_array \- Phasor array manipulation functions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B include "std/array.phs";
.PP
.B arr_push(array, value)
.B arr_pop(array)
.B arr_insert(array, index, value)
.B arr_resize(array, new_size)
.fi
.SH FUNCTIONS
.TP
.BR arr_push (array, value)
Append a value to the end of an array, mutating it in place.
.RS
.PP
.B Arguments:
.RS
.IP \fBarray\fR 12
Array to modify
.IP \fBvalue\fR 12
Value to append
.RE
.PP
.B Returns:
The same array (for chaining)
.PP
.B Throws:
Runtime error if the first argument is not an array
.RE
.PP
.TP
.BR arr_pop (array)
Remove and return the last element of an array, mutating it in place.
.RS
.PP
.B Arguments:
.RS
.IP \fBarray\fR 12
Array to modify
.RE
.PP
.B Returns:
The removed element (not the array)
.PP
.B Throws:
Runtime error if the argument is not an array, or if the array is empty
.RE
.PP
.TP
.BR arr_insert (array, index, value)
Insert a value at a specific position in an array, mutating it in place and shifting later
elements back.
.RS
.PP
.B Arguments:
.RS
.IP \fBarray\fR 12
Array to modify
.IP \fBindex\fR 12
Zero-based position to insert at. May equal the array's current length to insert at the end.
.IP \fBvalue\fR 12
Value to insert
.RE
.PP
.B Returns:
The same array (for chaining)
.PP
.B Throws:
Runtime error if the first argument is not an array, or if \fBindex\fR is negative or greater
than the array's current length
.RE
.PP
.TP
.BR arr_resize (array, new_size)
Resize an array in place, mutating it directly. Growing the array fills new slots with a
default (zero/empty/null-like) value for the array's element type; shrinking the array
discards trailing elements.
.RS
.PP
.B Arguments:
.RS
.IP \fBarray\fR 12
Array to modify
.IP \fBnew_size\fR 12
New length for the array
.RE
.PP
.B Returns:
The same array (for chaining)
.PP
.B Throws:
Runtime error if the first argument is not an array, or if \fBnew_size\fR is negative
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.B Basic Array Operations
.PP
.nf
.RS
include "std/array.phs";

var items = ["a", "b", "c"];
putf("Length: %d\n", arr_length(items));  // 3

arr_push(items, "d");
puts(items[items.len() - 1]);  // "d"

var last = arr_pop(items);
puts(last);  // "d"
.RE
.fi
.PP
.B Inserting and Resizing
.PP
.nf
.RS
include "std/array.phs";

var nums = [1, 2, 4, 5];
arr_insert(nums, 2, 3);  // nums is now [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]

arr_resize(nums, 3);     // nums is now [1, 2, 3]
arr_resize(nums, 5);     // nums grows back to 5 elements, new slots default-initialized
.RE
.fi
.PP
.B Chaining
.PP
.nf
.RS
include "std/array.phs";

var stack = [];
arr_push(arr_push(arr_push(stack, 1), 2), 3);
// stack is now [1, 2, 3]
.RE
.fi
.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
All functions in this module mutate the array argument in place rather than returning a copy
.IP \(bu 2
.BR arr_push() ", " arr_insert() ", and " arr_resize()
return the array itself so calls can be chained; \fBarr_pop()\fR is the exception and returns
the removed element instead
.IP \(bu 2
Array indices are zero-based
